NC Digital provides SEO and digital marketing for Porthcawl businesses. We help you rank higher on Google, show up in the map results, and get found by visitors and locals alike.

Need a website to support your marketing? See our [web design for Porthcawl and Bridgend businesses](/web-design-bridgend/).

## Digital marketing for a seaside town

Porthcawl's customers are a mix of locals and visitors. Visitors plan trips on Google before they arrive: "cafe Porthcawl", "surf lessons Rest Bay", "things to do in Porthcawl". Locals search for trades and services all year round. Both groups start with Google and Google Maps, so that is where your marketing effort pays back most.

Seasonal businesses in hospitality, holiday lets, food and leisure need to be visible before the busy months. Trades and services need steady enquiries all year.

## What our Porthcawl SEO and digital marketing includes

- **Local keyword research:** the searches visitors and locals use, including seasonal ones
- **Google Business Profile optimisation:** opening hours, photos, posts and reviews, the things visitors check first
- **Website pages that match searches:** clear pages for each service, product or experience
- **On-page and technical fixes:** titles, speed and mobile layout, since most visitors search on their phones
- **Local citations and links:** consistent listings on the directories and local sites people use
- **Monthly reporting:** calls, bookings, enquiries and rankings, in plain English

## What it costs

SEO starts from **£200 a month**, with a minimum of three months. For seasonal businesses, the best time to start is a few months before your busy season.

